{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#992","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#992","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#992\",\"parent_revision\":\"676768f3e4a28da58e3b5660d7a5263c932534bdb7677d8e4b225883d93b5a2c\",\"root_revision\":\"676768f3e4a28da58e3b5660d7a5263c932534bdb7677d8e4b225883d93b5a2c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ncomplete-implementation skill only accepts plan file paths (plan/P{NNN}-{slug}.yaml). When bug fixes are resolved without SAM plans (e.g., direct linting agent fixes for #988 and #989), there is no way to run the quality gate phases. The skill needs to accept issue numbers (#N) and run a proportional verification flow \u2014 at minimum: run tests on modified files, verify the fix, apply status:verified label. Without this, items get resolved without independent verification, creating unverified closures in the GitHub Issues backend.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claims Verified\\n\\n1. **\\\"complete-implementation only accepts plan file paths\\\"**: VERIFIED\\n   - Evidence: SKILL.md line 3 shows `argument-hint: <task-file-path>`. SKILL.md line 21-22 shows `<task_file> $ARGUMENTS </task_file>` \u2014 expects a file path argument. No code path handles issue number inputs directly as primary argument.\\n\\n2. **\\\"No way to run quality gates without SAM plan\\\"**: VERIFIED\\n   - Evidence: All quality gate phases in SKILL.md (lines 38-450) are triggered by extracting plan address (`P{N}`) from the task file path (lines 29-32). No alternative entry point exists that accepts issue numbers to initiate quality gates. Pre-Phase 1 mentions deriving issue number from plan's `issue` field or backlog item (lines 82-86), but issue number is discovered from the plan, not provided as input.\\n\\n3. **\\\"Direct linting agent fixes for #988 and #989 had no way to run quality gates\\\"**: INCONCLUSIVE\\n   - Evidence: `git log --grep='#988'` and `git log --grep='#989'` both returned only the commit `c6be9f78 fix(development-harness): resolve test collection errors and LSP violations` which does not mention either number in the subject. No explicit evidence found that #988 and #989 were fixed without SAM plans. Cannot verify or refute this claim without access to those issues or commits that mention them.\\n\\n4. **\\\"status:verified label exists and can be applied\\\"**: VERIFIED\\n   - Evidence: backlog_core/server.py lines 479-486 define `verified: Annotated[bool, ...]` parameter in `backlog_update` MCP tool. Description: \\\"Apply status:verified label to the GitHub issue. Signals that /complete-implementation quality gates have passed.\\\" SKILL.md line 475 calls `backlog_update(selector=\\\"{matched_item_title}\\\", verified=True)` to apply the label after completion verification gate passes.\\n\\n5. **\\\"The skill needs to accept issue numbers (#N)\\\"**: VERIFIED AS NECESSARY\\n   - Evidence: For non-SAM bug fixes (direct agent work without plans), there is currently no way to invoke quality gates since complete-implementation requires a plan file path. Adding issue number input would allow quality gates to be run on issues without SAM plans. This would resolve the constraint identified in claim #2.\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n- **VERIFIED**: 4 claims\\n  - complete-implementation accepts only plan file paths\\n  - No alternative entry to quality gates exists\\n  - status:verified parameter exists and is functional\\n  - Need for issue number input is justified\\n\\n- **INCONCLUSIVE**: 1 claim\\n  - #988 and #989 fix details (insufficient commit history visible)\\n\\n### Recommendation\\n\\nThe feature request is valid. Adding issue number input to complete-implementation would provide a way to run quality gates on issues that are resolved without SAM plans (e.g., direct agent linting fixes). The skill should accept `--issue` flag or similar parameter alongside the existing task file path argument.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: complete-implementation should accept issue numbers for non-SAM fixes\\nGoal: Allow /complete-implementation to accept issue numbers (#N) and run proportional quality gates for non-SAM fixes\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Current complete-implementation input parsing | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-checker verified SKILL.md takes task-file-path argument only, parses plan address from filename\\n2. Quality gate phases applicable without SAM plan | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Impact-analyst identified quality_gates.py build_quality_gate_plan() as the builder; proportional subset (code-review, test, verify) identified by groomer\\n3. How modified files determined from issue number | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: git log --grep=#N provides commit SHAs; git diff extracts modified files; backlog MCP provides issue metadata\\n4. status:verified label application | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-checker confirmed backlog_update verified=true parameter exists (server.py line 479-486)\\n5. Minimum verification flow | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Groomer defined 2-3 phase proportional flow in Expected Behavior section\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Conditions 1-3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker and impact-analyst agents)\\n- No new MISSING conditions discovered\\n- No conditions refuted\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Primary modification sites (from Impact Radius findings):**\\n\\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Add input routing (plan file vs #N detection), implement proportional gate builder dispatch, add conditional label application.\\n\\n- `/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 Add `build_proportional_quality_gate_plan()` function; modify `build_quality_gate_plan()` to conditionally invoke proportional builder when plan param is None.\\n\\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 Add conditional logic to handle missing context file (non-SAM fixes don't write context files); gracefully skip GitHub sub-issue sync when context file absent.\\n\\n**Documentation files (will become stale \u2014 must update):**\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Add Phase 0 (Input Routing), add Issue Number Mode section describing 2-3 phase flow, update Phase task mapping table with conditional agent selection.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Add decision diamond \\\"Input has plan file?\\\" \u2192 SAM path vs issue-only path branching.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (frontmatter) \u2014 Update `argument-hint` from `<task-file-path>` to `<task-file-path | #N | issue-number>`. Update description to include issue number acceptance.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Add note that complete-implementation now handles both SAM and issue-direct fixes.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 Clarify Step 8.5a accepts both plan paths and issue numbers.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/README.md` \u2014 Quality gates workflow section may need examples of both input formats.\\n\\n**Test files (need new coverage):**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` \u2014 Add test fixtures for issue-number inputs (with/without linked plan).\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 Add assertions for proportional gate plan structure.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 Add scenario \\\"bug fix via linting agent \u2192 complete-implementation #N\\\".\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py` \u2014 Add test coverage for backlog_view MCP calls with issue number.\\n\\n**Supporting files (if new agents needed):**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/generic-test-runner.md` (if new) \u2014 Runs tests on modified files for Phase 2 of proportional gates.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/issue-verification-gate.md` (if new) \u2014 Verifies issue acceptance criteria for Phase 3.\\n\\n**Configuration / CI:**\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/quality-gate-audit.yml` \u2014 If this workflow runs complete-implementation tests, verify test coverage includes both input formats.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Existing code patterns:**\\n\\n1. **Input routing pattern** \u2014 `/work-backlog-item` SKILL.md already implements issue number / plan path detection. See lines ~40-60 where it routes based on input format (`selector` parameter supports #N, bare number, or backlog item title). Use this as reference for implementing routing in complete-implementation.\\n\\n2. **Backlog MCP tool usage** \u2014 `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#{N}\\\")` is the canonical way to fetch issue data in the codebase. Already used by work-backlog-item, implement-feature, and other skills. Complete-implementation will use the same tool.\\n\\n3. **Quality gate plan builder** \u2014 `sam_schema.core.quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()` is the existing pattern for creating SAM-enforced quality gate plans (task-based dispatch loop). Proportional builder should follow the same structure but with simplified task list (3 phases instead of 6).\\n\\n4. **Status label application** \u2014 `backlog_update(selector=..., verified=true)` already exists and works. Backlog MCP tool handles label creation and application. Use directly, no new tooling needed.\\n\\n5. **Code reviewer agent** \u2014 `@dh:code-reviewer` is the existing agent for code review phases. Already used in SAM path (Phase 1). Reuse for proportional gate Phase 1 without modification.\\n\\n6. **Task status hook pattern** \u2014 `task_status_hook.py` already handles SubagentStop events and reads context files. Extend with conditional logic (try/catch on context file read) to support non-SAM fixes where context file is absent.\\n\\n7. **Test file patterns** \u2014 Existing test cases in `test_quality_gates.py` and `test_quality_gate_integration.py` use fixtures, parametrization, and SAM MCP mocking. Follow the same patterns for issue-number input test cases.\\n\\n**MCP tools available (no new tools needed):**\\n\\n- `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#{N}\\\")` \u2014 Fetch issue data (number, title, body, labels, plan field).\\n- `backlog_update(selector=\\\"#{N}\\\", verified=true)` \u2014 Apply status:verified label.\\n- `sam_create(slug=\\\"...\\\", goal=\\\"...\\\", tasks_yaml=\\\"...\\\")` \u2014 Create quality gate plan (used by proportional builder).\\n- `sam_status(plan=\\\"QG{N}\\\")` \u2014 Query quality gate plan status (used to verify all phases complete).\\n- `sam_ready(plan=\\\"QG{N}\\\")` \u2014 List ready tasks for dispatch (used in SAM path, unchanged).\\n- `sam_claim(plan=\\\"QG{N}\\\", task=\\\"T{M}\\\")` \u2014 Claim task before dispatch (used in SAM path, unchanged).\\n\\n**System documentation:**\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Comprehensive reference for complete-implementation phases, acceptance criteria, and SAM dispatch loop. Update with new Issue Number Mode section.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Data flow diagram showing current SAM-only path. Extend with issue-only path branching.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Current skill implementation. Reference for understanding existing 6-phase flow, hook configuration, MCP tool invocations.\\n\\n**Related code to review before implementation:**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 Lines ~40-60 show issue routing pattern. Lines ~250+ show AUTO_MODE invocation of complete-implementation (will be enhanced to accept issue numbers).\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Line ~180 shows SAM path invocation of complete-implementation. Remains unchanged, used as baseline for backward compatibility testing.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` \u2014 Existing test structure, fixtures, and mocking patterns. Model new test cases on existing ones.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Who / what is affected:**\\n\\n- **Developers using `/work-backlog-item` with AUTO_MODE** \u2014 Step 8.5a calls complete-implementation. Currently only works for SAM-based items. Issue-direct fixes cannot reach quality gates via this workflow.\\n\\n- **Direct agent fixes without SAM plans** \u2014 Linting fixes (#988, #989), bug fixes, and other single-agent implementations bypass quality gates entirely. No verification path exists. Examples: formatter corrections, typo fixes, simple refactorings.\\n\\n- **GitHub Issues backlog** \u2014 Unverified closures accumulate without status:verified label. Over time, the label system becomes corrupted (some verified, some unverified, no distinguishing factor).\\n\\n- **Quality assurance process** \u2014 The tooling presents an asymmetric verification story: planned work gets rigorous gates, unplanned fixes get none. This creates false assurance (verified only means \\\"had a plan\\\") and hidden risk (unplanned fixes may be higher-quality than planned ones, but are unmarked).\\n\\n- **Skill completeness** \u2014 complete-implementation is described as the \\\"final quality gate for any feature or fix\\\". Currently, it gates only SAM-based work. Issue-direct work is silently excluded from this description.\\n\\n**Scope of change from Impact Radius findings:**\\n\\n- **Code producers** \u2014 3 files: SKILL.md (input routing + proportional gates), task_status_hook.py (context file handling), quality_gates.py (conditional gate builder).\\n- **Code consumers** \u2014 3 direct callers (work-backlog-item, implement-feature, tests); 2 documentation files (local-workflow.md, workflow-architecture-diagram.md).\\n- **Documentation consumers** \u2014 6+ files will become stale and require updates (CLAUDE.md, README.md, step-procedures.md, process-audit docs, examples).\\n- **Tests** \u2014 4+ files need new test cases for issue-number inputs and proportional gate flows.\\n- **Agents** \u2014 No changes to existing agents; 2 new agents may be needed if proportional gates require specialized test runners or issue verifiers.\\n- **System connectivity** \u2014 No changes to SAM MCP or backlog MCP servers. complete-implementation will use existing `backlog_view` and `backlog_update` MCP tools.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n**PRIMARY CHANGE SITE:**\\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Currently accepts `$ARGUMENTS` as task-file-path only. Will need to:\\n  1. Add input routing logic to detect issue number vs plan file path format\\n  2. Support `#N`, bare number, or GitHub URL inputs (matching work-backlog-item pattern)\\n  3. Extract plan file path from issue metadata when issue number provided\\n  4. Implement proportional verification flow (condensed quality gates for non-SAM fixes)\\n  5. Handle cases where issue has no linked plan (direct linting/bug-fix scenarios)\\n\\n**SUPPORTING SCRIPTS:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 SubagentStop hook may need conditional logic based on completion source (SAM vs issue-direct). Currently assumes task_status_hook.py reads from context files set by start-task. Non-SAM fixes won't have context files. Hook should gracefully handle missing context.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 build_quality_gate_plan() currently designed for SAM task plans with acceptance-criteria-structured. Non-SAM fixes may not have this. Need conditional logic: if SAM plan exists, use full 6-phase gates; if issue-only, use proportional 2-3 phase gates (code review + test + verify).\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n**DIRECT CALLERS:**\\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` (Step 8.5a AUTO_MODE) \u2014 Invokes complete-implementation at end of SAM workflow. Will continue to pass plan file path. No change needed, but orchestrator logic must remain backward compatible.\\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Invokes complete-implementation when all tasks COMPLETE. Will continue to pass plan file path. Must remain backward compatible.\\n- Test files that mock complete-implementation behavior:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py`\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gates.py`\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py`\\n\\n**DOCUMENTATION CONSUMERS:**\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Comprehensive documentation of complete-implementation phases. Documents current input as task-file-path only. Will need new \\\"Issue Number Mode\\\" section with truncated gate phases and acceptance criteria for issue-only flow.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Data flow diagram showing complete-implementation as final stage. Will need branching for SAM vs issue-only paths.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n**MUST UPDATE:**\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Complete rewrite needed:\\n  - Add Phase 0: Input Parsing (detect issue vs plan, route to appropriate flow)\\n  - Phase 1-6 (SAM path) \u2014 unchanged, kept for backward compatibility\\n  - New Phase 1-3 (Issue-only path) \u2014 condensed gates: code review, test verification, labeled verification\\n  - Pre-Phase 1b: Process Accumulated Concerns \u2014 remains in both flows\\n  - Apply status:verified Label section \u2014 applies to both flows now\\n  - Final Step: Commit and Push \u2014 applies to both flows\\n  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Add decision diamond: \\\"Input has plan file?\\\" \u2192 YES: SAM dispatch loop (existing), NO: proportional gates (new)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` frontmatter and body:\\n  - Update `argument-hint` from `<task-file-path>` to `<task-file-path | #N | issue-number>`\\n  - Update `description` to include issue number acceptance\\n  - Add new \\\"Input Routing\\\" section documenting format detection and flow selection\\n\\n**INDIRECT STALE RISK:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Lists complete-implementation skill and its role in SAM. Add note that skill now handles both SAM and issue-direct fixes.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/README.md` \u2014 Quality gates workflow section may reference complete-implementation. Check if examples need issue-number variants.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 Step 8.5a (AUTO_MODE) describes calling complete-implementation. Must clarify that both file path AND issue number inputs are valid.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Closing section calls complete-implementation. Should remain unchanged but verify no hardcoded expectations about plan file paths.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n**GITHUB ACTIONS:**\\n- `.github/workflows/quality-gate-audit.yml` \u2014 If this workflow runs complete-implementation tests, verify test coverage includes both input formats.\\n\\n**TEST CONFIGURATION:**\\n- All test files referencing complete-implementation need parametrized test coverage:\\n  - `test_quality_gate_integration.py` \u2014 add test fixtures for issue-number inputs\\n  - `test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 add assertions for proportional gate selection\\n  - `test_scenarios.py` \u2014 add scenario for issue-direct bug fix flow\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n**QUALITY GATE AGENTS \u2014 NO CHANGES NEEDED:**\\n- `@dh:code-reviewer` \u2014 Remains unchanged. Called in both SAM and issue-only flows.\\n- `@dh:feature-verifier` \u2014 Remains unchanged (SAM flow only).\\n- `@dh:integration-checker` \u2014 Remains unchanged (SAM flow only).\\n- `@dh:doc-drift-auditor` \u2014 Remains unchanged (SAM flow only).\\n- `@dh:service-docs-maintainer` \u2014 Remains unchanged (SAM flow only).\\n- `@dh:context-refinement` \u2014 Remains unchanged (SAM flow only).\\n\\n**NEW AGENTS FOR ISSUE-ONLY FLOW:**\\n- `@dh:generic-test-runner` \u2014 NEW: Run tests on modified files for issue-direct fixes. Will be invoked in Phase 2 of proportional gates (replacing feature-verifier + integration-checker).\\n- `@dh:issue-verification-gate` \u2014 NEW: Verify that the GitHub issue acceptance criteria are met (simpler than TN verification, no baseline needed). Invoked in Phase 3.\\n\\n**ORCHESTRATION AGENTS:**\\n- `@dh:context-gathering` \u2014 May need to conditionally gather issue context vs plan context. If called from complete-implementation for issue-only flow, instruct to read issue body and extract acceptance criteria (if present) instead of searching for acceptance-criteria-structured in plan.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n**ENTRY POINTS (called from skill invocation):**\\n1. `/work-backlog-item` Step 8.5a (AUTO_MODE) \u2192 `/complete-implementation {plan_path}`\\n2. `/implement-feature` completion \u2192 `/complete-implementation {plan_path}`\\n3. User directly \u2192 `/complete-implementation {plan_path}` OR NEW: `/complete-implementation #992` OR `/complete-implementation 992`\\n\\n**PRODUCTION CODE (production execution path):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Skill entry point\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 Status tracking (SubagentStop hook)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 Quality gate plan builder (build_quality_gate_plan function)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 Backlog item CRUD (if fetching issue data)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 MCP server (if using backlog_view to fetch issue #N)\\n\\n**TEST CODE (test execution path):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gates.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 May test backlog_view used for issue number resolution\\n\\n**REFERENCE CODE (documentation/examples):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 Documents Step 8.5a invocation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/example-sessions.md` \u2014 May contain complete-implementation invocation examples\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/process-audit-backlog-lifecycle-2026-03-02.md` \u2014 May reference complete-implementation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` \u2014 May document quality gate workflow\\n\\n**RELATED SYSTEMS (dependency graph):**\\n- SAM MCP server (`mcp__plugin_dh_sam__*`) \u2014 Called by complete-implementation to query plan status, create quality gate plans, claim tasks\\n- Backlog MCP server (`mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*`) \u2014 Called by complete-implementation to fetch issue data (new path), update labels\\n- GitHub API (via backlog_core) \u2014 Underlying backend for all issue operations\\n- Git operations \u2014 Final commit+push step (unchanged)\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] complete-implementation SKILL.md: Add input routing (plan file vs #N / number / URL) with format detection\\n- [ ] complete-implementation SKILL.md: Implement issue-first path matching work-backlog-item pattern (selector \u2192 backlog_view \u2192 issue data)\\n- [ ] complete-implementation SKILL.md: Extract plan file path from issue when available, error gracefully when missing\\n- [ ] complete-implementation SKILL.md: Implement conditional quality gate selection (full 6-phase for SAM, proportional 2-3 phase for issue-direct)\\n- [ ] complete-implementation SKILL.md: Add proportional gate phases (code review + test + verify) with simplified verification (no T0/TN baseline, no doc drift audit)\\n- [ ] task_status_hook.py: Add conditional logic to handle missing context file (non-SAM fixes)\\n- [ ] quality_gates.py: Add build_proportional_quality_gate_plan() function for issue-only flow\\n- [ ] quality_gates.py: Modify build_quality_gate_plan() to conditionally invoke proportional builder when plan param is None\\n- [ ] local-workflow.md: Add \\\"Input Routing\\\" section documenting format detection\\n- [ ] local-workflow.md: Add \\\"Issue Number Mode\\\" section with 2-3 phase gate description\\n- [ ] local-workflow.md: Update \\\"Phase task mapping\\\" table to show conditional agent selection\\n- [ ] test_quality_gate_integration.py: Add test case for issue-number input with no linked plan\\n- [ ] test_quality_gate_integration.py: Add test case for issue-number input with linked plan (should auto-resolve)\\n- [ ] test_quality_gates.py: Add assertion for proportional gate plan structure\\n- [ ] test_scenarios.py: Add scenario \\\"bug fix via linting agent \u2192 complete-implementation #N\\\"\\n- [ ] workflow-architecture-diagram.md: Add decision diamond for input type detection\\n- [ ] backlog_view MCP tool: Ensure it returns issue data usable by complete-implementation (number, title, body, status, labels, plan field if present)\\n- [ ] Generic-test-runner agent (if new): Create or define agent for Phase 2 of proportional gates\\n- [ ] Issue-verification-gate agent (if new): Create or define agent for Phase 3 of proportional gates\\n- [ ] Complete-implementation examples: Update any hardcoded plan-file-path examples to show both formats\\n- [ ] Backward compatibility: Verify plan-file-path input continues to work unchanged (no breaking changes)\\n- [ ] Error handling: Add clear error messages when issue number is provided but issue does not exist, or issue exists but has no linked plan AND no acceptance criteria in body\\n\\n---\\n\\n**SCOPE SUMMARY:**\\n\\n- **Breaking change risk:** LOW (backward compatible \u2014 plan file path input unchanged)\\n- **Test coverage gaps:** MEDIUM (need new test cases for issue-number input and proportional gate flow)\\n- **Documentation drift risk:** HIGH (6 files reference complete-implementation workflow; new branching logic must be documented)\\n- **Agent dependency risk:** LOW (existing agents unchanged; new agents needed only if proportional gates require specialized code review or test runner)\\n- **Configuration risk:** LOW (no GitHub Actions or CI changes needed, test configuration only)\\n- **Impact scope:** 4 code files, 6+ documentation files, 4+ test files, 2 skill invocation points, 1 new decision path in SAM pipeline\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n### Priority\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**External systems (must be available):**\\n\\n1. **GitHub Issues API** \u2014 Via backlog MCP server and backlog_core operations. Used to fetch issue data (body, labels, metadata) and apply status:verified label. Must be functional for issue-number input path to work. Fallback: issue does not exist error.\\n\\n2. **Backlog MCP server** \u2014 Provides `backlog_view()` and `backlog_update()` tools. Must be available and healthy for issue number resolution and label application. If unavailable, error: \\\"Backlog MCP server not responding\\\".\\n\\n3. **SAM MCP server** \u2014 Used by proportional gate builder to create quality gate plans and dispatch phases. Must be available for both SAM path (existing) and issue-only path (new). If unavailable, error: \\\"SAM MCP server not responding\\\".\\n\\n4. **Git repository** \u2014 Issue-only path needs to determine modified files from commits linked to the issue. Uses `git log` or similar to find commits mentioning issue number. If git is unavailable, test verification phase cannot run.\\n\\n**Project-level conventions / systems:**\\n\\n1. **Status labels system** \u2014 The `status:verified` label must exist in GitHub repository labels. If missing, backlog MCP will auto-create it (feature exists in backlog_core). No explicit dependency.\\n\\n2. **Issue acceptance criteria convention** \u2014 Proportional gates expect acceptance criteria to be in issue body as \\\"## Acceptance Criteria\\\" header or bullet list. If issue has no criteria, Phase 3 (acceptance check) still passes (non-blocking). No blocking dependency.\\n\\n3. **Commit message convention** \u2014 Issue-only path uses commits to determine which files were modified. Commits should mention issue number (e.g., \\\"Fixes #992\\\") for git log filtering. If not present, tool may not correctly identify issue-related commits. No blocking dependency, but affects accuracy.\\n\\n**Skill-level dependencies:**\\n\\n1. **`/backlog` skill or backlog MCP server** \u2014 Must load and be functional for issue data fetching. Invoked by complete-implementation to fetch issue via `backlog_view()` and apply label via `backlog_update()`. Blocking dependency for issue-number path.\\n\\n2. **`/dh:sam` skill or SAM MCP server** \u2014 Must load and be functional for quality gate plan creation and dispatch. Used by both SAM path (existing) and proportional gate path (new). Blocking dependency for all paths.\\n\\n3. **Code reviewer agent (`@dh:code-reviewer`)** \u2014 Must be available for Phase 1 of proportional gates. Existing agent, unchanged. Blocking dependency for issue-only path Phase 1.\\n\\n4. **Test runner capability** \u2014 Phase 2 (test verification) runs tests on modified files. Requires test framework to be configured in the project (pytest, etc.). If no tests exist for modified files, phase passes trivially. Soft dependency.\\n\\n**Internal code dependencies:**\\n\\n1. **`sam_schema.core.quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()`** \u2014 Existing function that creates SAM task plans for quality gates. Proportional builder will be added as `build_proportional_quality_gate_plan()` in the same module. Depends on sam_schema being importable.\\n\\n2. **`task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler** \u2014 Already handles status updates when sub-agents finish. Will be extended to handle missing context files (non-SAM case). Depends on hook infrastructure being intact.\\n\\n3. **Backlog integration** \u2014 complete-implementation will call backlog MCP tools (`backlog_view`, `backlog_update`). These are already integrated in other skills. Soft dependency (tools exist, no new integration needed).\\n\\n**Testing / CI dependencies:**\\n\\n1. **Test fixtures for backlog_view() responses** \u2014 New test cases will need mock responses from backlog_view with various issue states (no plan, with plan, no acceptance criteria, etc.). Depends on test framework supporting mocking.\\n\\n2. **SAM MCP mock / sandbox** \u2014 Proportional gate tests will need to mock quality gate plan creation and dispatch. Depends on existing test infrastructure (test_quality_gate_integration.py).\\n\\n3. **GitHub Actions CI** \u2014 If quality-gate-audit.yml runs complete-implementation tests, it must be updated to cover both input formats. Depends on CI workflow being modifiable (no restrictions).\\n\\n**Risks / blockers:**\\n\\n1. **Issue data not available** \u2014 If issue number is provided but issue is deleted or private, backlog_view will fail. Graceful error handling required.\\n\\n2. **Plan file path and issue number ambiguity** \u2014 Input \\\"123\\\" could be interpreted as issue #123 or part of a file path. Clarify parsing rules: if input starts with \\\"plan/\\\", treat as file path; else treat as issue number.\\n\\n3. **Acceptance criteria parsing complexity** \u2014 Issue bodies are user-written prose. Parsing acceptance criteria may be fragile. Recommendation: accept any acceptance criteria in body as sufficient and allow Phase 3 to pass if criteria cannot be parsed (non-blocking approach).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Why P1:**\\n\\n1. **Blocks complete verification workflow for non-SAM fixes** \u2014 When agents directly implement simple fixes (linting errors, typos, single-file changes) without a SAM plan, there is currently no way to invoke quality gates. Issues get resolved without independent code review and verification, creating unverified closures.\\n\\n2. **Creates asymmetry in verification paths** \u2014 SAM-based features get 6-phase quality gates, but direct fixes (which may be more frequent in fast feedback loops) skip verification entirely. This inverts the risk profile: simple fixes should require LESS verification overhead, not NO verification.\\n\\n3. **Blocks AUTO_MODE in work-backlog-item** \u2014 The skill's Step 8.5a invokes complete-implementation at the end of SAM workflows. Without issue-number acceptance, the orchestrator cannot call complete-implementation on issues that were resolved via direct agent work. AUTO_MODE automation is incomplete.\\n\\n4. **Accumulating technical debt** \u2014 Issues resolved without status:verified label create a tail of unverified work in the backlog. Over time, this makes it impossible to distinguish verified from unverified fixes in GitHub Issues. The status becomes meaningless.\\n\\n5. **Opportunity for consolidation** \u2014 Both SAM and issue-direct paths should route through the same quality gate system. The system is currently dual-path with only one path implemented. Completing the second path eliminates a latent feature gap.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] **Input parsing** \u2014 `/complete-implementation` SKILL.md accepts and correctly routes three input formats: `#N`, bare number `N`, and plan file path `plan/P{NNN}-*.yaml`. Format detection is case-insensitive for issue prefix (# or bare).\\n\\n- [ ] **Issue data fetching** \u2014 When issue number is provided, skill fetches issue via `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#{N}\\\")` and extracts: number, title, body, labels, plan field (if present).\\n\\n- [ ] **Plan auto-resolution** \u2014 If fetched issue has non-empty plan field, skill extracts plan path and redirects to SAM path (6-phase gates). Backward compatible \u2014 plan path input behavior unchanged.\\n\\n- [ ] **Proportional gate selection** \u2014 If issue has no linked plan, skill routes to proportional 2-3 phase gates (code review + test + acceptance check). Full 6-phase gates used only for SAM path.\\n\\n- [ ] **Code review phase** \u2014 Phase 1 dispatches code-reviewer agent on issue-modified files. Agent produces review findings with no follow-up task file generation (simplified vs SAM path).\\n\\n- [ ] **Test verification phase** \u2014 Phase 2 runs tests on files modified by commits linked to the issue. Tests pass \u2192 phase succeeds. Tests fail \u2192 phase fails, user must fix and re-run.\\n\\n- [ ] **Acceptance criteria parsing** \u2014 Skill extracts acceptance criteria from issue body (looks for \\\"## Acceptance Criteria\\\" header or bullet list). If not found, warns user and allows phase 3 to pass (non-blocking).\\n\\n- [ ] **Acceptance check phase** \u2014 Phase 3 verifies issue acceptance criteria are met (or skips if no criteria found). Delegates to manual review or simple validation based on issue body content.\\n\\n- [ ] **Label application** \u2014 On successful completion (all phases pass), applies `status:verified` label via `backlog_update(selector=\\\"#{N}\\\", verified=true)`. Fails gracefully if label system unavailable (non-blocking).\\n\\n- [ ] **Error handling** \u2014 Clear error messages for: issue not found, issue without plan AND no acceptance criteria, test failures (with logs), phase failures (with findings).\\n\\n- [ ] **Backward compatibility** \u2014 Plan file paths (plan/P{NNN}-*.yaml) continue to work unchanged. Existing callers (work-backlog-item, implement-feature) produce no test failures.\\n\\n- [ ] **Test coverage** \u2014 Add test cases for:\\n  - Issue-number input with no linked plan \u2192 proportional gates run\\n  - Issue-number input with linked plan \u2192 SAM gates run (auto-resolved)\\n  - Issue-number input with plan file that does not exist \u2192 error\\n  - Issue that does not exist \u2192 error\\n  - Plan file path input (backward compat) \u2192 SAM gates run unchanged\\n  - Proportional gate phases succeed \u2192 status:verified label applied\\n  - Proportional gate phase fails \u2192 correct phase failure reported, no label applied\\n\\n- [ ] **AUTO_MODE integration** \u2014 `/work-backlog-item` Step 8.5a invocation works for both SAM-planned items and issue-direct items. Both routes produce status:verified label on success.\\n\\n- [ ] **Documentation** \u2014 Update `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` and `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` with new \\\"Issue Number Mode\\\" section documenting proportional gate flow, input routing, and conditional logic.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Invocation:**\\n\\n```bash\\n/complete-implementation #992\\n# or\\n/complete-implementation 992\\n# or (backward compatible)\\n/complete-implementation plan/P001-example.yaml\\n```\\n\\n**Flow diagram:**\\n\\n```\\nUser invokes: /complete-implementation {input}\\n  \u2193\\nPhase 0: Input Routing\\n  \u251c\u2500 Detect input type (plan file vs issue number)\\n  \u2502\\n  \u251c\u2500 IF plan file path (plan/P{N}-*.yaml):\\n  \u2502  \u2514\u2500 Extract plan number P{N}\\n  \u2502     \u2193\\n  \u2502     [SAM path \u2014 use existing 6-phase gates]\\n  \u2502     \u2192 Query SAM MCP: sam_status(P{N})\\n  \u2502     \u2192 Verify all implementation tasks COMPLETE\\n  \u2502     \u2192 Read TN verification report\\n  \u2502     \u2192 Dispatch Quality Gate Plan (QG{N})\\n  \u2502     \u2192 Apply status:verified label\\n  \u2502     \u2192 Commit + push\\n  \u2502\\n  \u2514\u2500 IF issue number (#N or bare N):\\n     \u2514\u2500 Fetch issue via backlog MCP: backlog_view(selector=\\\"#{N}\\\")\\n        \u2193\\n        Has linked plan field?\\n        \u251c\u2500 YES: Extract plan path\\n        \u2502  \u2514\u2500 [Recurse to SAM path above]\\n        \u2502\\n        \u2514\u2500 NO: Proceed to proportional gates\\n           \u2193\\n           [Issue-only path \u2014 use simplified 2-3 phase gates]\\n           \\n           Pre-Phase: Fetch issue acceptance criteria\\n             \u251c\u2500 If issue body contains \\\"## Acceptance Criteria\\\" section \u2192 parse\\n             \u251c\u2500 Else if issue body contains bullet list of criteria \u2192 parse\\n             \u2514\u2500 Else \u2192 warn \\\"No acceptance criteria found in issue body\\\"\\n           \\n           Phase 1: Code Review\\n             \u251c\u2500 Delegate to code-reviewer agent\\n             \u251c\u2500 Agent reviews modified files (from git commits on this issue)\\n             \u2514\u2500 Returns findings (no follow-up task files for issue-only flow)\\n           \\n           Phase 2: Test Verification\\n             \u251c\u2500 Run tests on files modified by commits linked to issue\\n             \u251c\u2500 Pass criteria: all tests pass, no regressions\\n             \u2514\u2500 Fail criteria: test failures, coverage gaps\\n           \\n           Phase 3: Issue Acceptance Check\\n             \u251c\u2500 Verify issue acceptance criteria are satisfied\\n             \u251c\u2500 Compare acceptance criteria against code changes\\n             \u2514\u2500 Pass criteria: all listed criteria met; fail criteria: any unmet\\n           \\n           Post-phases: Apply label + commit\\n             \u251c\u2500 All phases pass \u2192 apply status:verified label via backlog MCP\\n             \u251c\u2500 Any phase fails \u2192 STOP, report failures, ask user to fix\\n             \u2514\u2500 On success \u2192 commit modified files (issue update)\\n```\\n\\n**Errors and recovery:**\\n\\n- **Issue does not exist** \u2014 Error: \\\"Issue #N not found. Verify issue number and run again.\\\"\\n- **Issue exists but no linked plan AND no acceptance criteria in body** \u2014 Error: \\\"Issue #N has no linked plan and no acceptance criteria in body. Cannot run quality gates. Options: (1) add acceptance criteria to issue body, or (2) create a SAM plan.\\\"\\n- **Code review phase fails** \u2014 Report findings, stop. User fixes and re-runs `/complete-implementation #N`.\\n- **Test verification phase fails** \u2014 Report test failures, stop. User fixes and re-runs.\\n- **Acceptance criteria check fails** \u2014 Report unmet criteria, stop. User addresses and re-runs.\\n\\n**Backward compatibility:**\\n\\n- Plan file paths (plan/P{NNN}-*.yaml) continue to route to the existing 6-phase SAM workflow without change.\\n- `/implement-feature` and `/work-backlog-item` continue to call `/complete-implementation {plan_path}` unchanged.\\n- All existing tests for SAM path remain passing.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Estimate: Medium (4-5 implementation tasks)**\\n\\n**Justification:**\\n\\n1. **Input routing logic** (0.5 task)\\n   - Pattern already exists in work-backlog-item. Implement format detection (plan file vs #N) and conditional dispatch.\\n   - Scope: Single function in SKILL.md, ~20-30 lines of logic.\\n   - Complexity: Low \u2014 straightforward regex or string parsing.\\n\\n2. **Proportional quality gate plan builder** (1 task)\\n   - Add `build_proportional_quality_gate_plan()` function in quality_gates.py.\\n   - Task structure: 3 phases (code review, test verification, acceptance check) instead of 6.\\n   - Dependencies: Simpler than SAM builder \u2014 no T0/TN baseline, no doc drift audit.\\n   - Scope: ~150-200 lines of Python code.\\n   - Complexity: Medium \u2014 requires understanding SAM task plan structure, but is a simplified variant.\\n\\n3. **complete-implementation SKILL.md enhancement** (1.5 tasks)\\n   - Modify skill to add issue-number input path, dispatch to proportional gates when needed.\\n   - Enhance hook configuration or add new context handling for non-SAM fixes.\\n   - Refactor SKILL.md body to support branching (SAM vs issue-only path).\\n   - Scope: ~100-150 lines of skill logic (add branching to existing ~450 lines).\\n   - Complexity: Medium \u2014 branching logic, conditional MCP tool invocations, error handling.\\n\\n4. **task_status_hook.py enhancement** (0.5 task)\\n   - Add conditional logic to handle missing context file (issue-direct fixes don't write context files).\\n   - Gracefully skip GitHub sub-issue sync when context absent.\\n   - Scope: ~10-20 lines of error handling.\\n   - Complexity: Low \u2014 add try/except blocks.\\n\\n5. **Test coverage** (1 task)\\n   - Add test cases for issue-number input (with/without plan, non-existent issue).\\n   - Add test cases for proportional gate flow (all phases pass, phase failures).\\n   - Parametrize existing SAM tests to ensure backward compatibility.\\n   - Scope: ~80-120 lines of test code across 3 test files.\\n   - Complexity: Medium \u2014 requires mocking backlog_view responses, quality gate plan creation, and SAM dispatch.\\n\\n6. **Documentation** (0.5 task)\\n   - Update `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` with Issue Number Mode section.\\n   - Update SKILL.md frontmatter (argument-hint, description).\\n   - Update workflow-architecture-diagram.md with decision diamond.\\n   - Scope: ~150-200 lines of documentation.\\n   - Complexity: Low \u2014 documentation, not code.\\n\\n**Task decomposition estimate:**\\n\\n- **T1** \u2014 Implement proportional quality gate plan builder (quality_gates.py)\\n- **T2** \u2014 Enhance complete-implementation SKILL.md with input routing and branching\\n- **T3** \u2014 Add test coverage for issue-number input (test_quality_gate_integration.py)\\n- **T4** \u2014 Update documentation (local-workflow.md, workflow-architecture-diagram.md, SKILL.md frontmatter)\\n- **T5** \u2014 Bug fixes and edge case handling (as discovered during implementation)\\n\\n**Risks that could increase effort:**\\n\\n1. **Acceptance criteria parsing in issue bodies** \u2014 If acceptance criteria are frequently formatted inconsistently (bullet lists vs headers vs narrative prose), parsing may require more sophisticated logic (NLP or template matching). Mitigation: Start simple (look for specific headers/markers), accept non-blocking failures.\\n\\n2. **Modified file detection from issue number** \u2014 Git commit history may not always mention issue number. Determining which files are \\\"issue-related\\\" may be ambiguous. Mitigation: Run tests on all modified files in recent commits, accept over-broad scope.\\n\\n3. **Test framework integration** \u2014 If test runner is not configured or tests are sparse, Phase 2 may be trivial. Mitigation: Document that Phase 2 passes trivially if no tests found (non-blocking).\\n\\n4. **Documentation drift** \u2014 Multiple files reference complete-implementation. Keeping all documentation in sync may be time-consuming. Mitigation: Automated sync scripts or centralized reference (MASTER DOC in SKILL.md frontmatter).\\n\\n**Confidence level:** 75% (Medium confidence)\\n- Proportional gates are simpler than SAM 6-phase gates, reducing implementation risk.\\n- Existing backlog MCP and SAM MCP tools already provide needed functionality.\\n- Backward compatibility constraint is clear and testable.\\n- Documentation is comprehensive but creates maintenance burden.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Steps to trigger the gap:**\\n\\n1. Work on a bug fix or direct linting fix without creating a SAM plan (e.g., direct agent implementation of a linting fix).\\n2. Resolve the issue and commit the changes.\\n3. Attempt to run quality gates via `/complete-implementation #N` (where N is the issue number).\\n4. **Observed**: Skill rejects input with error: \\\"Expected task file path (plan/P{NNN}-{slug}.yaml), got #N\\\".\\n5. Quality gate phases do not run. The fix is not independently verified. The issue is resolved without status:verified label applied.\\n\\n**Current workaround (if attempting quality gates on non-SAM fix):**\\n- Must manually create a stub SAM plan with acceptance criteria, then invoke `/complete-implementation {path}`. This is tedious and defeats the purpose of direct agent fixes for simple issues.\\n- Alternative: Skip quality gates entirely and resolve the issue without verification label. This creates unverified closures in GitHub Issues.\\n\\n**Desired behavior:**\\n- User invokes `/complete-implementation #992` or `/complete-implementation 992`.\\n- Skill accepts the input, fetches issue data from GitHub, runs proportional quality gates (code review + test verification + issue acceptance check).\\n- On success, applies status:verified label and closes with confirmation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **complete-implementation should accept issue numbers for non-sam fixes** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 attempted /complete-implementation #988 and #989, skill rejected non-plan input\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**In Scope:**\\n\\n1. **Input routing logic** \u2014 Detect whether input is a plan file path (plan/P{NNN}-*.yaml) vs issue number (#N, bare number N, or GitHub URL).\\n2. **Issue data resolution** \u2014 Fetch issue from GitHub using backlog MCP `backlog_view` tool. Extract issue number, title, body, acceptance criteria (if present), and linked plan field (if any).\\n3. **Conditional gate selection** \u2014 If issue has linked plan file \u2192 use full 6-phase quality gates (SAM path, unchanged). If issue has no plan \u2192 use proportional 2-3 phase gates (issue-only path, new).\\n4. **Proportional quality gates for issue-only fixes** \u2014 Simplified verification flow: Phase 1 (code review), Phase 2 (test verification on modified files), Phase 3 (issue acceptance criteria check). No T0 baseline, no TN verification, no doc drift audit.\\n5. **Backward compatibility** \u2014 Plan file path input must continue to work unchanged. No breaking changes to existing `/implement-feature` or `/work-backlog-item` callers.\\n6. **Label application** \u2014 Apply status:verified label on successful completion via backlog MCP `backlog_update(verified=true)`.\\n7. **Error handling** \u2014 Clear error messages when issue does not exist, or issue exists but has no linked plan AND no acceptance criteria in body (insufficient information to run verification).\\n8. **Test coverage** \u2014 Add test cases for issue-number input with/without linked plan, and proportional gate flow.\\n\\n**Out of Scope:**\\n\\n1. **Creating new SAM plans from issue data** \u2014 If an issue has no linked plan and no acceptance criteria in body, do NOT automatically generate a plan. Error gracefully.\\n2. **Modifying SAM plan creation** \u2014 sam_create behavior remains unchanged. Issue-only fixes do not produce SAM plans.\\n3. **New quality gate agents** \u2014 Use existing code-reviewer agent. If new agents are needed (generic-test-runner, issue-verification-gate), defer to follow-up implementation task.\\n4. **Custom verification logic per issue type** \u2014 Proportional gates apply the same 2-3 phase flow to all issue-direct fixes. No branching based on issue labels, type, or other metadata.\\n5. **Retroactive labeling of closed issues** \u2014 This feature gates quality gates on new invocations. It does not scan closed issues and retroactively apply labels.\\n6. **Integration with GitHub PR workflows** \u2014 Issue-number input assumes issue is resolved via commits, not PRs. PR-based workflows continue to use plan files.\\n7. **Pre-completion status label application** \u2014 Pre-commit checks, draft labels, and other intermediate statuses remain unchanged. Only status:verified is applied at the final gate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] quality_gates.py _proportional_phase_body uses if/elif \u2014 Not confirmed: code passes all linting, match-case is style preference not defect\\n- [x] Coverage config points at scripts/ not plugins/ \u2014 Confirmed pre-existing issue, backlog item created\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/PATTERNS.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-03-22T15:43:38.661462+00:00 |\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-complete-implementation-issue-numbers.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-22T15:45:18.309814+00:00 |\\n| 